{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A semiring (S, ⊕, ⊗, 0̄, 1̄), the algebra of path problems (Mohri 2002; Gondran–Minoux 2008)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Semiring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SQ","text":"Equatable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"⊗ extends a path by an edge and ⊕ combines alternative paths. The shortest-path entry points in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPaths answer a different question for each conformer. The tropical semiring gives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest paths, the bottleneck semiring widest paths, the Boolean semiring reachability, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counting semiring the number of paths.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A conformer implements the four requirements. The type system does not check the laws, and an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm’s result is meaningful only when they hold:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊕ is associative and commutative, with identity "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":";"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"⊗ is associative, with identity ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"one"},{"text":";","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":" annihilates: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a ⊗ 0̄ == 0̄ ⊗ a == 0̄"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ distributes over ⊕ from both sides."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ need not be commutative. Algorithms always compute "},{"code":"distance ⊗ weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in path order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not "},{"code":"AdditiveArithmetic.zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". No semiring type here is a number, and a tropical"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is +∞."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operators "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊕"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊗"},{"type":"text","text":" call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plus(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"times(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", so the two spellings always agree."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Prefer the methods where another module might declare the same operators, and inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":". That macro folds an expression without these operators’ precedences, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a ⊕ b == c)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not type-check, while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a.plus(b) == c)"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-2ou28","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-93rtg"],"anchor":"Operators"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings